<title>BRAZIL: ACPC said already agreed on coffee export cut.</title>
<headline>ACPC said already agreed on coffee export cut.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Members of the Association of Coffee Producing Countries (ACPC) have already agreed on a minimum cut in coffee exports in the first half of this year, the Ugandan Trade and Industry Minister told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be a cut. We have already agreed on a minimum. All we are trying to do today is improve the minimum,&quot; Abel Rwendeire said prior to an ACPC meeting.</p>
<p>Rwendeire added that the minimum was not less than one million 60-kg bags and involved arabica and robusta cuts.</p>
</text>
